## 5. The CSC-F1 caveat transfers — DPSA-F6 NOT discharged

**Status: binding.**

`H_δ` is an energy/measure-type certificate. Nothing in the inertial bases sees **tree structure**: inertia, like the trace moments, is **split-blind**. Grounding DPSA on inertial bases therefore does **not** discharge **DPSA-F6** — the `D_branch` slot stays empty until an explicitly branch-sensitive term exists. The Guth–Wang–Bateman–Zahl lesson holds in this register too: density-and-energy statistics do not see trees.

